      "hint": "Expand mentally: what is the degree? For intercepts, use the Zero Product Property directly on the factored form.",
      "solution_steps": [
        "Expand: (x+3)(x−5) = x² − 2x − 15. Highest power = 2 → parent is quadratic.",
        "Zero Product Property: set each factor = 0.",
        "x+3 = 0 → x = −3.",
        "x−5 = 0 → x = 5.",
        "No squaring, no ±. Factored form gives roots DIRECTLY. This is why form matters."
      ],
      "feedback_correct": "🔥 Quadratic intercepts nailed.",
      "feedback_wrong_parent": "Expand: what is the highest power of x?",
      "feedback_wrong_intercepts": "Set each factor = 0 separately. Zero Product Property.",
      "feedback_wrong": "Set f(x)=0. Zero-product: x=-3 or x=5."
